'''Line B''' of the [[CristoCarril]] (CC) system is a commuter rail line operated by [[Intercon]] that runs on the [[Portnou Line]] corridor between the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and the [[Estació Central de Portnou]] in [[Portnou]]. The line covers 100.0 km and serves 25 stations across three comarcas — [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|Sant Cristòfor]], [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]], and [[Marjal del Canal (comarca)|Marjal del Canal]] — before terminating at Portnou. It is the second-longest CristoCarril route after [[Line A (CristoCarril)|Line A]].

Line B follows the inland route southward from the Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal, through the eastern ciutats of Sant Cristòfor, the inland municipalities of Cumará, and the canal corridor of Marjal del Canal. The line shares the Portnou Line tracks with [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 3, which provides local services within the Portnou metropolitan area.

== Route ==

=== Sant Cristòfor ===

Line B begins at the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], the city's primary rail hub. From the terminal, the line heads south through three stations in Original — [[Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station|Portal de Sant Cristòfor]], [[Sant Pere (CristoCarril)|Sant Pere]], and [[La Font (CristoCarril)|La Font]] — serving the dense residential neighbourhoods south of the historic core. The line then enters [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], where it stops at [[Dàrsena Est (CristoCarril)|Dàrsena Est]], the only Dàrsena station on the Portnou Line (the western Dàrsena stations are served by [[Line A (CristoCarril)|Line A]] on the Coastal Line).

Continuing south, the line passes through two stations in [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]] — [[Sant Martí Nord (CristoCarril)|Sant Martí Nord]] and [[Sant Martí Sud (CristoCarril)|Sant Martí Sud]] — and three stations in [[Sant Llorenç (ciutat)|Sant Llorenç]] — [[Sant Llorenç Nord (CristoCarril)|Sant Llorenç Nord]], [[Sant Llorenç Centre (CristoCarril)|Sant Llorenç Centre]], and [[Sant Llorenç Sud (CristoCarril)|Sant Llorenç Sud]]. The line then enters [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]], serving three stations — [[Ciutat de l'Estació Nord (CristoCarril)|Ciutat de l'Estació Nord]], [[Ciutat de l'Estació Centre (CristoCarril)|Ciutat de l'Estació Centre]], and [[Ciutat de l'Estació Sud (CristoCarril)|Ciutat de l'Estació Sud]]. The 13 stations within Sant Cristòfor cover the eastern and southern coastal plain of the city, serving the dense residential and commercial districts south and east of the historic core. The Ciutat de l'Estació stations form a key commuter pair with the Enllaç stations in Cumará, with heavy peak-period ridership in both directions.

=== Cumará ===

After leaving Sant Cristòfor, Line B enters the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]] and serves the city of [[Enllaç]], the second-largest municipality in Cumará with a population of over 633,000. The line stops at four stations in Enllaç: [[Central Enllaç (CristoCarril)|Central Enllaç]], the city's main rail hub; [[Vessant (CristoCarril)|Vessant]]; [[Carretera de Sant Joan (CristoCarril)|Carretera de Sant Joan]]; and [[Carretera del Magatzem (CristoCarril)|Carretera del Magatzem]]. The Enllaç stations form a commuter pair with the Ciutat de l'Estació stations in Sant Cristòfor, generating significant bidirectional peak-period traffic. The line then serves [[Els Horts (CristoCarril)|Els Horts]], the main station in the municipality of [[Els Horts]] (pop. 60,624).

=== Marjal del Canal ===

The line enters the [[Marjal del Canal (comarca)|Marjal del Canal comarca]] at [[Sant Mateu Est (CristoCarril)|Sant Mateu Est]], a station on the eastern edge of [[Sant Mateu, Marjal del Canal, Estret|Sant Mateu]] near the Riu Burutí. The next two stations are in [[La Portella]] — [[La Portella Nord (CristoCarril)|La Portella Nord]] and [[La Portella Sud (CristoCarril)|La Portella Sud]] — followed by [[La Marjal (CristoCarril)|La Marjal]] in the municipality of [[La Marjal]]. The line then enters [[Les Drassanes]], stopping at [[Les Drassanes Est (CristoCarril)|Les Drassanes Est]] in the eastern part of the municipality (the western Les Drassanes stations are served by Line A on the Coastal Line).

=== Portnou ===

After passing through Les Drassanes, Line B enters [[Portnou]], stopping at [[El Coll (CristoCarril)|El Coll]] in the northern neighbourhood of [[El Coll]] before running non-stop to the [[Estació Central de Portnou]], the city's principal rail hub. The intermediate stations between El Coll and the Estació Central — Montbau, Horta Nord, Horta, La Sagrera, and Centre — are served by [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 3 on the same Portnou Line tracks. The stations south of the Estació Central — Sud Ciudad, Moll de Baix, and Canal — are also served by Rodalies Line 3.

