== Service pattern ==

Line B operates four service patterns between [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Portnou]]:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Stops !! Stations served !! Travel time
|-
| '''Short''' || All stops 1–15 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Vessant || ~56 min
|-
| '''Limited''' || 1, 2, 5, 6, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Vessant, skipping minor intermediate stations || ~47 min
|-
| '''Express''' || 1, 2, 5, 12, 14, 24, 25 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Estació Central de Portnou, skipping intermediate stations || ~84 min
|-
| '''Local''' || All stops 1–25 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Estació Central de Portnou || ~111 min
|}

The '''short''' service operates within the Sant Cristòfor–Cumará commuter corridor, running from the Central Terminal through the southern and eastern ciutats to Vessant in Enllaç. This is the most frequent service, providing high-capacity commuter rail for the dense residential districts of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]], [[Sant Llorenç (ciutat)|Sant Llorenç]], [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]], and the northern Enllaç suburbs.

The '''limited''' service provides a faster alternative within the same corridor, stopping at nine key stations between the Central Terminal and Vessant. The limited skips the minor intermediate stations in Sant Pere, La Font, Sant Martí Sud, and the Sant Llorenç stations, serving the highest-demand stations only. This service caters to commuters travelling between the major residential nodes and the Central Terminal, and between the Ciutat de l'Estació and Enllaç commuter pair.

The '''express''' service provides the fastest connection between Sant Cristòfor and Portnou, stopping at the Central Terminal, Portal de Sant Cristòfor, Dàrsena Est, Ciutat de l'Estació Centre, Central Enllaç, El Coll, and the Estació Central de Portnou. The express skips most suburban stations and all intermediate stations in outer Cumará and Marjal del Canal, reducing the end-to-end journey to approximately 84 minutes. The express is primarily used by long-distance commuters between the two cities and passengers connecting to intercity services at Central Enllaç.

The '''local''' service stops at all 25 stations along the full 100.0 km route, with an end-to-end journey time of approximately 111 minutes (1 hour 51 minutes). The local provides the only CristoCarril service to the intermediate stations in Cumará (Carretera de Sant Joan, Carretera del Magatzem, Els Horts) and the Marjal del Canal municipalities (Sant Mateu Est, La Portella Nord, La Portella Sud, La Marjal, Les Drassanes Est). Within [[Portnou]], the local stops only at [[El Coll (CristoCarril)|El Coll]] before terminating at the Estació Central de Portnou; the intermediate stations — Montbau, Horta Nord, Horta, La Sagrera, and Centre — are served by [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 3 on the same Portnou Line tracks.

== Schedule ==

Line B operates from approximately 5:00 AM to 12:30 AM daily. Frequencies vary by service pattern and time of day:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Peak (7–10 AM, 4–7 PM) !! Off-peak (daytime) !! Evening (after 8 PM) !! Weekend
|-
| '''Short''' || every 10 min || every 15 min || every 20 min || every 20 min (daytime), every 30 min (evening)
|-
| '''Limited''' || every 15 min || every 20 min || every 30 min || every 30 min (daytime), every 45 min (evening)
|-
| '''Express''' || every 20 min || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 30 min (daytime), every 60 min (evening)
|-
| '''Local''' || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 90 min || every 60 min (daytime), every 90 min (evening)
|}

The short and limited services are the most frequent, reflecting the high commuter demand within the Sant Cristòfor–Enllaç corridor. The express provides a regular connection between the two cities and the intermediate hubs, with reduced evening and weekend frequency. The local is the least frequent, reflecting the lower ridership at the intermediate stations in outer Cumará and Marjal del Canal. Combined, the four services provide up to 15 trains per hour at the Central Terminal during peak periods.

== Fares ==

Line B uses the [[Tarifa Integrada]] zonal fare system, which is shared across the CristoCarril network and integrated with the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Rodalies de Portnou]] systems. The line crosses five fare zones:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Zone !! Stations !! Fare (B$)
|-
| 1 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to La Font (stations 1–4) || 2.50
|-
| 2 || Dàrsena Est to Sant Llorenç Sud (stations 5–10) || 3.75
|-
| 3 || Ciutat de l'Estació Nord to Carretera del Magatzem (stations 11–17) || 5.25
|-
| 4 || Els Horts to La Marjal (stations 18–22) || 6.50
|-
| 5 || Les Drassanes Est to Estació Central de Portnou (stations 23–25) || 7.75
|}

Fares are calculated based on the number of zones travelled through. Passengers using a [[Tarifa Integrada]] smart card receive free transfers to connecting metro, streetcar, and Rodalies services within a 90-minute window. Concession fares (half price) are available to seniors, students, and children under 12. Children under 5 travel free. Monthly and weekly passes are available with discounts of up to 40% off the single-ride fare.

